[00:00.00] How do you do, ladies and gentlemen?
[00:04.00] My name is Alfred Hitchcock,
[00:07.00] and this is music to be murdered by.
[00:12.00] It is mood music in a jugular vein,
[00:16.00] and I hope you like it.
[00:19.00] Our record requires only the simplest of equipment,
[00:24.00] an ordinary phonograph needle,
[00:28.00] a four-inch speaker,
[00:31.00] and a 38-caliber revolver.
[00:35.00] Naturally, the record is long playing,
[00:39.00] even though you may not be.
[00:42.00] So why don't you relax,
[00:44.00] lean back and enjoy yourself,
[00:47.00] until the coroner comes.
